KG42.register("rules-fdc9771bcf6ee99a8667e06f",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R015","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R015","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The benchmark's local market product is PV energy supplied within the microgrid. Scope: Cournot-model local microgrid market benchmark.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Cournot-model local microgrid market benchmark.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The benchmark's local market product is PV energy supplied within the microgrid. Scope: Cournot-model local microgrid market benchmark.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix B Cournot Model","anchor_text":"the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model. As referring to model of [28]–[30], ","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Cournot model was applied in the electricity market with multiple producers (i.e., power plants). We have reformulated the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model. As referring to model of [28]–[30], the players in the local market are only limited to seller role prosumers, the relation between selling prices and amount of energy is\np_s = a - bE^s. \\quad (31)\nIf E^s = 0, there is no PV energy that can be supplied in the microgrid. Therefore, the selling price should be equal to the price of utility grid \\lambda^b. If E^s \\ge E^b, the selling energy is more than the required energy. Then, the selling price should be minimized to \\lambda^s. Thus, the price function (31) should include the points (0,\\lambda^b) and (E^b,\\lambda^s), and the parameter a and b can be obtained\na = \\lambda^b, \\quad b = (\\lambda^b - \\lambda^s)/E^b. \\quad (32)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule only identifies what the local market product is in the Cournot benchmark. Evidence v141-b-g03-E12 does not define an independently chosen decision variable or its optimization domain for this product rule; the energy quantity E^s is used in the separate Cournot pricing relation and its aggregate definition is outside this rule's frozen graph and evidence. Adding a variable here would require importing scope from another rule.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter, coefficient, bound, or numeric value is stated for the product designation in this rule. Symbols such as a, b, λ^b, λ^s, and E^b belong to the Cournot pricing relation, not to this product-identity constraint, and assigning them here would duplicate the pricing rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E12","quote":"We have reformulated the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E12","quote":"If E^s = 0, there is no PV energy that can be supplied in the microgrid."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"ab33e8dc407fc9bbf2ab5ec908bc1b527db33cda1ad012590d3258d5f40ab801","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"This rule is a definitional market-scope statement: it identifies the Cournot benchmark's local market product as PV energy supplied within the microgrid. The supplied evidence (v141-b-g03-E12) uses E^s as an energy amount in the Cournot selling-price relation and states the boundary case E^s = 0, but it does not provide a standalone product equation, domain, unit, or independently optimized decision variable for product.local_energy. Formalizing a quantity here would require importing the separate aggregate-selling-energy definition and pricing scope from other rules, which this frozen rule does not contain. The existing phi therefore remains a procedural product designation, not a source-supported mathematical constraint.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
